From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gamesave: ask the host at a save conflict; file saves play
 locally offline

At a sync, a container that changed here and in the cloud since the last
sync (dirty, and the listing's clientFileTime is not the one last synced)
failed the whole sync with E_GS_CONTAINER_NOT_IN_SYNC: the session then
played on local saves and the conflict stayed until something forced a side
(XODUS_SAVE_SYNC=download/upload). Nothing asked the player.

cloud_sync now asks about each conflicting container through
SaveTransport::Conflict, which sends the host a SaveConflictRequest (Scid,
Container, DisplayName, LocalTime, CloudTime and CloudDevice, the listing's
deviceName when it has one) over the keyed bridge as message type 0x5001,
and waits for the player, as a game waits on the system's dialog. Each
container is its own question and its answer is for that container alone.
The reply is parsed as XML within the size the bridge gives (it is not
NUL-terminated), with no DTD and no network; only the root's <Choice>
counts:
- local: the cloud's container is first downloaded whole into a
  .recovery-cloud- copy beside the .recovery- copies a download keeps of
  the local side; only then are the local blobs uploaded over the cloud's
  (force_upload). If the cloud's side cannot be kept, nothing is uploaded
  and the container is left as for no answer.
- cloud: the cloud's container is downloaded, the local tree kept as a
  .recovery- copy as for any download.
- anything else, or no host: both sides kept. The other containers still
  sync; the sync then reports E_GS_CONTAINER_NOT_IN_SYNC, so this session
  plays on local saves, the dirty index kept, and the next connected
  session asks again.

The file-save provider (XGameSaveFiles) failed outright when the cloud
could not be reached or locked. Like the container provider (cloud_disable)
it now plays on local saves for the session, its changes left dirty for the
next connected one.

tests/Nexus/gamesave-sync.cpp covers, for both providers: the question's
fields, no host, an unanswered question, a reply whose choice lies past
its stated size, the local choice (the cloud's side kept whole first, then
an upload attempted, the local data still unsynced when it fails), the
local choice when the cloud's side cannot be kept (nothing uploaded, no
partial copy), the cloud choice (downloaded and synced), and two
conflicting containers asked separately and answered differently. Its
required check count rises to 407. The save tests link nexus-xml2 for the
parser's headers.

Playport's lines in this patch are offered under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-xbox-save-conflict-runtime.md
Offered-upstream: no
